# Secrets
.env
# Variants a deployment tends to create (.env.local, .env.production) hold the
# same keys. The PreToolUse hooks already treat these names as secret, and the
# two should agree. The example file holds only names, and is tracked.
.env.*
!.env.example
# `.streamlit/` is tracked for config.toml (the theme). secrets.toml is the
# conventional home for API keys in a Streamlit app, sits in that same now-
# tracked directory, and `git add .streamlit` would take it along.
.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Generated proposals. Real applications contain sensitive organizational and
# personnel data -- keep them out of git by default.
applications/

# Discovery scans. Same reasoning: a scored shortlist quotes the organization
# profile back, so it carries the same data the drafts do -- plus a record of
# which funders were considered and rejected, which is nobody else's business.
opportunities/

# The organisation profile. Same reasoning again, and the agent writes to it on
# its own: it records confirmed facts there, so the first real run puts the
# organisation's data in this file. It is created from templates/org-profile.md,
# which is what is tracked. Ignoring it is only half the fix -- git keeps
# tracking a file it already tracks, which is why the template was moved.
memories/org/AGENTS.md

# Persisted checkpoint (conversation/todo state) written by the CLI.
.grant_writer/

# Eval and performance-run output. It carries raw model output, and the
# graph-level runs write whole drafts built from the fixtures.
evals/out/

# Per-developer Claude Code context. `.claude/settings.json` is tracked on
# purpose -- its hooks and ty baseline are project rules everyone gets. These
# are the opposite: personal notes, and permissions approved on one machine.
# Claude Code writes settings.local.json itself the first time a permission is
# allowed for the project, so it turns up without being asked for.
.claude.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Tooling
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
